# Allowlist. The image gets only what the app and its tests need; everything
# else in the working folder (private business documents, the nested frontend
# clone, venvs, build output, worktrees) stays out by default. A denylist that
# "mirrors .gitignore" drifted: about 25 .gitignore entries never reached it.
# Adding a new top-level file or folder the app needs? Add a "!" line here;
# tests/test_deploy_config.py checks the required paths are included.
*
!app.py
!run.py
!requirements.txt
!pyproject.toml
!setup.py
!Dockerfile
!render.yaml
!.dockerignore
!README.md
!QUICKSTART.md
!FEEDBACK.md
!LICENSE
!integrity_engine
!trust_domain
!replay
!tests
!data
!docs/LESSONS.md
!docs/DATA_HANDLING_BOUNDARY.md
!docs/DEMO_GUIDE.md
!docs/ONBOARDING.md
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
# Never ship caches, even inside allowed folders
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
